WIRE.md §6.1, §6.6: load.csv with `header: true` builds a list, keyed list or table of records, never an optional one; load.dir a list, keyed list or table, never an optional one (§6.5); with `format:` naming text or csv, each element is what that format builds (§6.7, §6.6: a String, or `[[String]]`, load.dir having no header).
-- a/a.canon --
package a

local record Row {
  name: String
}

local let ints: [Int] = load.csv("@resource/a.csv", header: true)
local let maybe: [Row]? = load.csv("@resource/a.csv", header: true)
local let keyed: [Row] keyed by name = load.csv("@resource/a.csv", header: true)
local let byName: table Row = load.csv("@resource/a.csv", header: true)

local let dirMaybe: [Row]? = load.dir("@resource/rows/*.json")
local let dirRows: [Row] keyed by name = load.dir("@resource/rows/*.json")
local let dirTable: table Row = load.dir("@resource/rows/*.json")
local let texts: [String] = load.dir("@resource/rows/*.txt", format: text)
local let textRows: [Row] = load.dir("@resource/rows/*.txt", format: text)
local let grids: [[[String]]] = load.dir("@resource/rows/*.csv", format: csv)
local let csvRows: table Row = load.dir("@resource/rows/*.csv", format: csv)
